This directory contains the cards used by the MadGraph5_aMC@NLO
fNLO fixed-order calculation.

Processes with on-shell decay chains additionally contain decay_card.dat.
That card controls the physical widths, decay
renormalization scales, and the production renormalization-scale momentum
choice. Full NLO production-and-decay bundles use separate LO and NLO
total widths for each corrected species. Their default ADDITIVE combination
uses a strict fixed-order O(alpha_s) expansion. Its narrow-width denominators
use the LO entries; the
NLO-minus-LO differences enter only through the linear Born counterterm. That
counterterm counts physical resonance occurrences, independently of which
partial-decay numerators receive QCD corrections.

Cards use the usual `value = parameter ! explanation` syntax and document all
options in place. There is no version field or END record; older card syntaxes
are not supported. Launch calculate_xsect NLO for mixed orders and select

  NLO = production_order
  NLO = decay_order

Set either to LO to disable its corrections. Optional species overrides use
`LO = decay_perturbative_order(6)`. Decay order also selects LO/NLO total
widths; calculate_xsect LO selects LO everywhere. NLO_DECAY_COMBINATION can
be ADDITIVE (strict NLO expansion) or MULTIPLICATIVE (product of blocks).

For decay-scale reweighting, set

  CORRELATED = decay_scale_variation_mode
  1.0, 2.0, 0.5 = decay_scale_factors

Use CORRELATED to identify the decay factors with rw_rscale; the factor lists
must then match exactly and in the same order. Use INDEPENDENT for the full
Cartesian product of production muR, production muF, and one factor per
distinct scale-dependent decay species. The first factor must be 1. Every
point is retained as a separate weight in the final HwU, labeled by production
muR/muF and each decay d<PDG> factor. With production reweight_scale enabled,
INDEPENDENT includes production-only, decay-only and simultaneous variations
in a single run; it does not replace these weights by an envelope. Every
non-central point also varies the total width. For an alpha_s-independent
Born decay, AUTO = decay_width_scale_mode(6) keeps the LO width constant and
runs the NLO-minus-LO correction by alpha_s(mu)/alpha_s(decay_ren_scale(6)).
The supplied LO total width must also be alpha_s independent. For other
decays use EXPLICIT mode and supply, for example,

  1.49 = lo_decay_width_variation(6, 2.0)
  1.37 = nlo_decay_width_variation(6, 2.0)

at each noncentral factor (with physical values appropriate to the process).
NLO entries are required only for species kept at NLO. AUTO and EXPLICIT
must not be mixed for one species. All widths are TOTAL widths in GeV.

Event-by-event scales use decay_dynamical_scale_choice(PDG): 0 fixed,
1 sum daughter ET, 2 sum daughter mT, 3 half the mT sum, -1 the editable
fixed_user_decay_scale hook in SubProcesses/dummy_fct.f90. These choices
use the block's immediate daughters in the event frame and apply a 2 GeV
floor before variation factors. They require an alpha_s-independent Born
decay and AUTO widths: each occurrence's width follows its own scale.
decay_ren_scale(PDG) remains the reference for the supplied LO/NLO widths.

The run-card switch cut_decays controls whether built-in and user-defined
generation cuts see forced-decay products. It defaults to false; fixed-order
analyses always see the complete decayed event.
